# Kompis CORE approval creation & discovery

## Authority

- Authoritative decision lives in `CORE.APPROVAL` via `action_requests`.
- `kompis_operator_approvals` is mirror/history only — never unlocks execution alone.
- Local Kompis approve cannot decide publish/rollback.

## Creation contract

- Approval-required website publish/rollback steps must create or fetch CORE approval during `create_app_kompis_operator_run`.
- Run/step may show `awaiting_approval` / “Venter på godkjenning” only when a valid `action_request` + binding exist.
- No awaiting approval without CORE approval.
- If creation fails: controlled error, no false pending, execution stays blocked, retry available.
- Creation must be idempotent; concurrency must not duplicate approvals.
- Scope (tenant, run, step, tool, website, path, candidate/version) is server-resolved.

## Discovery contract

- The same approval ID must appear in Kompis and Approval Center.
- Deep link must open the exact approval (`/app/approvals?request=<id>`), never an empty generic list when an ID exists.
- Notifications are not approvals.
- Expired, cancelled, rejected, and consumed approvals are not pending.

## UX

- One clear card: “Godkjenning kreves” → primary “Gjennomgå og godkjenn”.
- No competing local “Godkjenn og utfør” for CORE-gated runs.
- Nontechnical copy; no raw tool keys as primary titles; no raw enums/ISO in primary UI.
- Status capitalization comes from i18n data — never CSS `capitalize`.
- No English leakage in Norwegian locale for approval surfaces.

## Forbidden

- No UnoNight hardcoding.
- No customer hardcoding in Core.
- No auth/session/MFA handling changes.
- No live publish/rollback as part of repair verification.
- No local-authority bypass of CORE.APPROVAL.
